  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Cook rice: Rinse the rice until the water runs clear. Put in a small saucepan with 250ml (1 cup) water, cover and bring to a simmer over medium heat. Reduce the heat to low and cook for 12 mins or until tender and the water is absorbed. Turn off the heat and stand, covered, for at least 5 mins. Fluff the rice with a fork.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1574926/photos/large/66890_1-5df9bce76ca1548db9135684da69e407.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Meanwhile, crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1574927/photos/large/66890_2-ee96bd76d6744776ade1118dbd66f242.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Brown chicken-style strip: Heat 20g butter in a medium deep frypan over medium-high heat. Add the chicken-style strips, garlic and curry powder and cook, stirring, for 3-4 mins until browned and warmed through.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1574928/photos/large/66890_3-44b72cdf2421b48c2462af68bae7428b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer curry: Add the coconut milk, 2 tsp soy sauce, 1 tsp white vinegar, ½ tsp sugar and 80ml (⅓ cup) water to the chicken mixture. Season with salt and pepper and bring to a simmer. Reduce the heat to medium-low, cover and cook for 10 mins to develop the flavour.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1574929/photos/large/66890_4-7399490a9cce757e72b0c173cb20a757.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the peas to the curry and bring to the boil. Cook for 2 mins or until tender. Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper. Divide the rice and curry among bowls. Scatter over the fried shallots and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1574930/photos/large/66890_5-ebf8b44292a82762240b1584d44c3cea.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it spicy: Our curry is made with mild Malaysian spices, so it's great for the whole family. If you prefer a spicy kick, serve with a scattering of chopped fresh chilli or chilli flakes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1574931/photos/large/66890_6-474517471e7ece4d7702d69a44e9eb10.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
